/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
# generated CycloneDX SBOMs (cargo cyclonedx) + coverage reports — CI artifacts,
# never committed.
*.cdx.json
/lcov.info
# cargo-mutants local output, written by `scripts/mutants-audit.sh` (on-demand;
# there is no CI mutation job). Never committed.
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old
# Python bytecode caches. The gate's own `ci-gate`/`dashboard` legs run
# `python3 -m unittest`, which writes these; ignoring them keeps the content-hashed
# gate key (scripts/gate-key.sh hashes tracked + untracked-but-not-ignored files)
# from being perturbed mid-run, which would otherwise print `NOT RECORDED`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The filled bring-your-own-backends env file: it names your endpoints and may carry
# credentials. The .example template IS committed.
.env.external

# The operator's filled service and provider configs. These are the default discovery names
# (`crates/core/src/config/mod.rs`), README and docs/deployment.md tell operators to create
# them, and they hold a Vault token and S3 access keys by design — the same reasoning that
# ignores `.env.external` above. Nothing on the commit path scans for secrets (the
# pre-commit hook runs fmt, clippy and script-tests, not gitleaks), so an unignored
# `node.toml` is one `git commit -a` away from a committed credential. The shipped templates
# (`node.example.toml`, `node.quickstart.toml`, `tool.example.toml`) are committed and
# unaffected: they carry `<SET ME: …>` placeholders, not real values.
/node.toml
/tool.toml

# Artifacts the README quickstart writes into the checkout: `gdi-dataset-tool build -o build`
# and the `{id}.state.json` visibility sidecar. scripts/gate-key.sh content-hashes tracked
# AND untracked-but-unignored files, so following the quickstart in the repo otherwise
# perturbs the gate key mid-run and prints `NOT RECORDED` — the same failure the
# `__pycache__` entry above exists to prevent.
/build/
/*.state.json

# local key material / scratch
*.c4gh
*.c4gh.pub
# ...but keep checked-in test fixtures (self-generated / reference-authored
# known-answer vectors, not real data) for the Python-free crypt4gh regression
# guards.
!crates/core/tests/fixtures/crypt4gh/*.c4gh
!crates/core/tests/fixtures/crypt4gh_kat/*.c4gh
# ...and the tiny self-generated crypt4gh fuzz seed (not real data).
!crates/core/fuzz/corpus/crypt4gh_header/*.c4gh

# Editor and tool scratch inside the checkout, and generated fuzz corpora
.claude/
corpus/

# The S3 stack node identity is a secret key — never commit it.
compose/keys/*
!compose/keys/.gitkeep

# Local developer linker override (mold). Machine-specific: committing it would break any
# contributor without mold installed, and cargo config has no conditional form. The
# recommended place for it is the user-level ~/.cargo/config.toml, so worktrees inherit it
# (scripts/dev-setup.sh); a per-checkout copy stays ignored here so a leftover cannot be
# committed.
/.cargo/config.toml
.worktrees/
